             [1;38;2;231;233;238mHow will people sign in?[m             
                                                  
[38;2;216;180;90m▸[m [38;2;231;233;238mLocal accounts[m                                                    
[38;2;124;134;153m    People get a password managed by Orbit. Nothing else to set up.[m 
[38;2;124;134;153m    A provider can be added later with configure.sh.[m                
                                                                    
  [38;2;124;134;153mSingle sign-on (SSO) with an identity provider[m                    
[38;2;124;134;153m    People sign in through your OIDC provider — Authentik, Keycloak,[m
[38;2;124;134;153m    Entra ID and the like. Orbit asks for its address and client[m    
[38;2;124;134;153m    details next. Local accounts stay available as well.[m            
                                                                    
